Acceptance criteria:
  The docs/roadmap.md first-slice scenario passes on disposable test data.
  Voice remains available while a request runs without model-based status polling.
  No fabricated reads, false completion, unrestricted tools or duplicate dispatch.
  Playback interruption is separate from task cancellation.
  Proposed runtime isolation is demonstrated, not inferred from different paths.
  Human voice/visual acceptance is recorded separately from automated checks.
  Profile changes apply at a request boundary without changing running jobs,
  permissions or approved providers; default performance meets agreed budgets.
  Host authority, request/outbox transactions and snapshot resynchronization
  follow docs/runtime-contracts.md; browser mocks are not native-app evidence.

Completion evidence:
  Fixture sub-slice: Electron 45.2.1, React/TypeScript/Vite and Three.js; exact
  dependency lock, local build and launch commands in README/docs/prototype.md.
  npm run lint and npm run build pass; seven Vitest cases and six Playwright
  desktop scenarios pass. Actual Electron captures have alpha-zero corner
  pixels and visible mesh pixels; both workspace/floating screenshots inspected.
  Mode toggling, original bounds, hover/keyboard restoration, pinning, sandbox/
  context isolation, narrow preload actions, profile snapshots/persistence,
  explicit targets, terminal cancellation, honest completion, WebGL loss and
  idle/minimized frame scheduling are covered using disposable profiles.
  Native minimize/show events supplement browser visibility for rendering pause.
  Local system-voice output is optional/off by default; no listening assessment.
  Added exact-device selection/persistence, immediate track cleanup, camera
  denial, missing-device and access/enumeration failure checks using fake media.
  All six scenarios pass against the packaged executable. The portable EXE
  itself separately passes startup, ASAR UI, microphone check and floating
  restoration. Its inspected archive has seven runtime files; notices included,
  private stores/profiles/credentials/tests excluded. EXE is unsigned, x64 only.
  Published v0.1.0-prototype.1 (nondraft prerelease), source
