  README presentation sub-slice: 432 px rotating spherical mesh and vertically
  clipped, simulated microphone fill; 144 frames, 20 fps, 7.2-second loop.
  Shared-palette GIF is 4004733 bytes; original runtime icons remain unchanged.
  README contains centered linked images, with captioned actual packaged
  screenshots and synthetic-context disclosure. docs/guide.md preserves the
  former README content, rebasing links; it retains release/security warnings,
  workflow limits, setup and documentation navigation. tools/render_readme.py
  reproduces artwork locally with Pillow, without audio, sessions or a network.
  Reviewed representative animation frames and desktop/mobile HTML previews.
  Asset/link/anchor checks, exact text preservation, loop timing/seam and
  sub-5 MB budget pass. Isolated Edge verifies a 432 px desktop / 350 px mobile
  square, no narrow-screen overflow and still/GIF media selection. This is a
  local GitHub-like preview, not live GitHub rendering or human acceptance.
  No runtime/release changes, live agent prompt, app restart or new publication.

  Node-inspection source sub-slice: actual context-marker picking and the voice
  hub reveal compact transient labels; click/tap pins name/subtitle/base path.
  Arrow/Home/End keyboard inspection, Enter/Space pinning and close/Escape/
  same-node/blank dismissal preserve the work target. Orbit/pan drags do not
  pin; decorative fixture dots remain anonymous. Anchors follow camera/drift/
  resizing, clamp within the viewport and hide off-screen. First Escape closes
  a label before floating restoration while retaining speech cancellation.
  Lint/type/build, eight Vitest and six focused source Electron cases pass
  on disposable profiles. Actual pointer picking, keyboard/pin/dismissal,
  unchanged routing, zoom tracking, 360 px floating fit, orbit distinction,
  WebGL loss and pinned idle/minimize/drift scheduling are covered. Reviewed
  the narrow floating capture. No new dependency or continuous idle frame loop.
  This is local source, not a new package or published .7 feature. Existing
  user instances, microphones, actual agent sessions and releases are untouched.

